# Machine memory guard (required for all test commands)

The rules themselves are in `AGENTS.md` → **Memory Guard**, and the shared
reference is linked from `docs/agent-process-guard.md`. Read those; this rule
exists to make them always-applied in Cursor and to record the one
Cursor-specific fact:

- `.cursor/hooks.json` registers `beforeShellExecution` →
  `tools/agent-guard/guard-agent-command.mjs --protocol=cursor`, which blocks
  unguarded test entrypoints mechanically. Hooks are a recent Cursor feature — if
  a Cursor version does not honor them, the npm scripts are still guarded and
  only the direct-binary bypass reopens, which is why the written rule has to
  stand on its own too.
